From: cube oakley <cube-oakley@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 00:21:50 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] libcamera: simple: Add the Pixel 7 Pro cameras

The pixel-camera driver exposes each Pixel 7 Pro (GS201) camera as a raw
Bayer sensor feeding a CSIS write-DMA capture node, with no hardware ISP
in the path, so run the software ISP on it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
index d28d094..874cba1 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -265,6 +265,7 @@ static const SimplePipelineInfo supportedDevices[] = {
 	{ "j721e-csi2rx", {}, true },
 	{ "mtk-seninf", { { "mtk-mdp", 3 } }, false },
 	{ "mxc-isi", {}, false },
+	{ "pixel-camera", {}, true },
 	{ "qcom-camss", {}, true },
 	{ "sun6i-csi", {}, true },
 };
